{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgn4m6qpqGrjxKDtefMJa", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No. As far as the pipeline goes, nobody has been told about it.\n\n- **Nightly run:** it crashed at the line that creates the findings folder, before the alert step. So it never wrote the finding or queued an alert. The log confirms that, ending with \"FAILED, nothing published\".\n- **My work:** I didn't run the batch. There's no `spool/` folder in this checkout, so nothing is waiting for the relay to pick up. The tests did create alert files, but they went to a temporary folder and were addressed to `@example.com` test recipients, not the real ones.\n\nSo the security on-call, agent-safety and the pager haven't heard about the severity-3 finding (the agent writing to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json`). It's been unreported since the 2026-11-04 run, and they won't hear about it until the batch is rerun with alerts on or someone tells them directly.\n\nThere's one thing I can't check: whether anyone told them outside the pipeline, like Priya or whoever saw the failed run. I don't have access to that."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c01aed7b-7cfb-4db3-b5d6-4e6c3ec9ba33", "uuid": "f53a8acd-38ef-4fba-9cd9-88dee1e8cf42", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T17:26:02.223Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgn4m6cBRZQ5sSAcXhfkx"}
